# Deployment profile

The approved target is a standalone OCI container with Docker Compose as the default local
orchestration format. Version {{TEMPLATE_VERSION}} does not create a Dockerfile or Compose
service because this project has not selected a runtime.

When the runtime is approved, the deployment profile should define:

- a minimal trusted base image pinned by digest and rebuilt for security updates;
- locked Python and system dependencies using a multi-stage build;
- non-root execution, a read-only filesystem where feasible, and external durable volumes;
- explicit health and readiness checks plus CPU, memory, and restart limits;
- narrowly scoped network access and runtime-injected secrets;
- one primary concern per container, separating agents, MCP servers, databases, and
  untrusted-code sandboxes when their permissions differ; and
- deterministic image build, test, provenance, and rollback commands.

Do not put secret values in Compose files, build arguments, image layers, or the build context.
